# GNASHER — a charging animal for the FPS roster. Not a soldier, not a demon
# lord: a big brutish mass of meat whose whole argument is WEIGHT and a MAW.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE. There is no reference mesh and no reference plate for
# this character — by owner instruction, deliberately. So `blob:measure` and
# `blob:rings` do not apply (they exit 2 without a reference), and NO number
# below is "measured": every one is a design decision. The comment on each
# non-obvious number says WHY it is what it is, which is the house rule for a
# character with no mesh to fit against.
#
# WHO IT IS. A pack animal grown too big: it leads with its shoulders, it runs
# on its knuckles when it wants to close, and its skull is mostly mouth. It is
# not clever and it is not a species — it is what the arena sends when the
# grunts are not enough. It reads at distance as a wedge of muscle moving at
# you, and up close as a jaw with legs.
#
# THE FIVE BEATS, made concrete:
#   1. MASS FIRST. The chest is the deepest mass on the body (deep 1.45) and
#      the shoulder yoke is the widest thing on the creature (wide 1.90). The
#      hips are deliberately narrow, so the top-heavy read survives any yaw.
#   2. THE MAW IS THE FACE. The skull is three masses: a small cranium high and
#      back, a wide upper jaw, and a dropped lower jaw. The gape between the
#      jaws is ~0.10 m tall and 0.40 m wide — wider than the cranium — with
#      interlocking teeth as GEOMETRY (they are far too big and too central to
#      paint; the painted-face road is the documented failure, face.ts's
#      header).
#   3. SMALL LIT EYES. Two emissive prims (r 0.026) tucked under a heavy brow
#      shelf. The contrast between a tiny eye and a 0.40 m maw is what makes
#      the head read as an ANIMAL rather than a person with a big mouth.
#   4. HORNS AND FOREARM TUSKS are the only mesh parts (gnasher-kit.wam):
#      short horns swept BACK along the skull — NOT up and out (that is the
#      minotaur's silhouette, and the brief forbids it) — and ivory tusks
#      breaking out through the forearm flesh, pointing down-forward like
#      spurs.
#   5. ARMS THAT REACH THE GROUND. The arm chain is 1.40 m on a 1.90 m
#      creature; the fist masses bottom out ~0.09 m above the floor. Hanging
#      forward and low, they read as legs the animal has not committed to yet.
#
# STANCE. Declared `digitigrade`: the thigh is near-vertical, the shin pitches
# forward so the knee sits BEHIND the hip-to-ankle chord, and the long foot
# bone runs down-forward to a toe pad on the ground (the gargoyle's bird fold,
# which checkStance verifies). Omitting `stance` would mean "not checked", not
# "humanoid".
#
# NOT THE OTHER ROSTER HEAVIES. No horns that wrap up-and-out (minotaur), no
# machinery of any kind (cyberdemon), no wings or tail (gargoyle), no bovine
# muzzle. The skull is a mouth first and a face second.
model gnasher
  # 1.90 m of flesh, but the READ is the 0.60 m shoulder span and the 0.40 m
  # maw, not the height. Taller than this and the top-heavy wedge stops
  # reading as an animal; shorter and it reads as a fat humanoid.
  height 1.90
  stance digitigrade

skeleton
  # Hip line at 0.72 (root 0.58 + len 0.14; children attach at the TAIL).
  # 0.38 of height — the legs are SHORT for the bulk above them, which is the
  # brief's "barely adequate" beat. The pelvis LEN restores the crotch-to-hip
  # segment WAM's root (a bare point) does not have; see goblin-kit.wam.
  root pelvis at 0.58 len=0.14

  # Hunched chain, ~36 deg of forward lean to the shoulders and ~62 to the
  # skull: the head rides AHEAD of the hips and below the shoulder tops, which
  # is the charging posture. The neck is short and thick (0.13) on purpose —
  # a long neck would make this a quadruped that stands up; this one never
  # fully lifts its head.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=22 len=0.42
  bone chest parent=spine  dir=up pitch=14 len=0.40
  bone neck  parent=chest  dir=up pitch=20 len=0.13
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=6  len=0.30

  mirror
    # Shoulder socket at x ~0.27, y ~1.49, just proud of the chest's ~0.23
    # half-width. tilt=12 lifts the yoke into the neck (a brute's trap slope,
    # not a coat hanger) and the 0.28 reach is what makes the shoulders read
    # as ENORMOUS rather than as a wide chest.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    dir=side tilt=12 len=0.28
    # Arm chain 0.60 + 0.56 + 0.24 = 1.40 m. PITCH IS DELIBERATELY SMALL
    # (8/8/16): a steeply pitched arm shortens its vertical drop, and this
    # character's arms have to REACH THE GROUND. tilt=16 splays the upper arm
    # out so the elbow clears the deep chest — the goblin's arm-meld lesson.
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=8 tilt=16 len=0.60
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down pitch=8 tilt=6  len=0.56
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=16         len=0.24
    # Digitigrade, the dragon/gargoyle solution: near-vertical thigh (8),
    # shin pitched forward (16) so the knee falls BEHIND the hip->ankle chord,
    # then a long foot bone (64) down-forward to a toe joint at the ground.
    # Hip (0.15, 0.72) -> knee (0.231, 0.373, +0.049) -> ankle (0.231, 0.133,
    # +0.118) -> toe (0.231, 0.045, +0.298); knee offset -19 mm = digitigrade.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=8  tilt=13 side=0.15 len=0.36
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=16           len=0.25
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=down pitch=64           len=0.20
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — four masses. Kept NARROW in x (half-width ~0.23 at the chest) and
  # DEEP instead: the goblin paid twice for a wide torso whose arms then read
  # as bulges, and this character's arms are already fat. A brute's mass lives
  # in depth anyway, and the profile is what sells the charge.
  # ============================================================
  # Haunch: the seat the legs root into. Narrower than the chest on purpose so
  # the figure is top-heavy; wide 1.30 = 0.24 half-width.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.45 r=0.185 wide=1.30 tall=1.05 deep=1.15 blend=0.018
  # Waist: cinched to ~0.19 half-width so there is a break between haunch and
  # chest. Without it the three masses blend into one barrel.
  blob torso on spine at=0.30 r=0.170 wide=1.10 tall=1.05 deep=1.20 blend=0.018
  # Chest: the biggest single mass and the deepest thing on the body. r 0.210
  # x deep 1.45 = 0.305 half-depth against 0.231 half-width — a slab, not a
  # barrel.
  blob torso on chest at=0.40 r=0.210 wide=1.10 tall=1.20 deep=1.45 blend=0.018
  # Shoulder yoke: the widest mass on the creature (0.304 half-width, 0.70
  # tall) so the head can sink between the shoulders and read as small. This
  # is the "enormous shoulders carried ahead" beat.
  blob torso on chest at=0.95 r=0.160 wide=1.90 tall=0.70 deep=1.10 blend=0.014
  # Pectorals: two slabs on the chest front. `both` mirrors offset.x, so one
  # line makes the pair; without them the deep chest reads as a drum.
  blob torso on chest at=0.60 r=0.100 wide=1.25 deep=0.80 blend=0.010 offset=(0.085,0.015,0.155) both

  # ============================================================
  # NECK — a thick short column (r 0.105 against the zombie's 0.045). A brute
  # has no visible neck; this is the fattest one that still fuses the skull to
  # the yoke without the head floating.
  # ============================================================
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.105 deep=0.90 blend=0.008

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — the knuckle-dragger reach. One heavy mass per segment plus a blunt
  # fist and a knuckle bar. `core` on the deltoid: it is the structural mass
  # the fuse probe must use, and the fist blob below is fatter than the shaft
  # taper (the house core rule).
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.06 r=0.175 blend=0.014 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.12 to=0.95 r=0.150 r2=0.115 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.125 r2=0.095 blend=0.009 mirror
  # Fist: a blunt block, slightly deeper than wide (a fist is). The mass at
  # the far end is deliberate — this is the limb the animal walks on.
  blob arm on hand at=0.55 r=0.145 wide=1.10 tall=0.95 deep=1.20 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Knuckle row: one bar across the front-bottom of the fist. `both` is
  # unavailable (mirror), so the bar is centred and the fist's own width does
  # the splay.
  bar  arm on hand from=0.85 to=1.05 r=0.045 r2=0.030 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0,-0.05,0.075) mirror

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — digitigrade: fat thigh, slim shin, swollen hock, long metatarsus,
  # three-toed ground pad with claws. The leg is SHORT (0.72 hip line) against
  # a 1.40 m arm: that ratio is the "runs on all fours when it wants to" read.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.05 r=0.155 blend=0.012 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.10 to=0.95 r=0.150 r2=0.100 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.095 r2=0.075 blend=0.009 mirror
  # Calf: a mass at the BACK of the shin (offset -z) — without it the shin is
  # a cone and the leg reads as a peg.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.30 r=0.090 wide=1.00 tall=1.10 deep=0.85 blend=0.009 offset=(0,-0.010,-0.050) mirror
  # Hock: the swollen heel joint at the shin's tail.
  blob leg on foot  at=0.02 r=0.100 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Metatarsus: the long forward column down to the toe joint.
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.10 to=0.85 r=0.085 r2=0.070 tall=1.10 deep=0.95 blend=0.010 mirror
  # Toe pad: the ground-contact fan. offset y +0.02 lifts the sole to y ~0.01
  # (bone tail 0.045, r 0.080 x tall 0.70 = 0.056 semi-height).
  blob leg on foot  at=1.00 offset=(0.030,0.020,0.040) r=0.080 wide=1.40 tall=0.70 deep=1.50 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Claws: centre plus one splayed line, dark and chamfered to points. The .r
  # foot's reflected offsets put the second at the mirrored x, so each foot
  # shows a splayed pair around the centre claw.
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.98 to=1.10 r=0.035 r2=0.006 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.030,-0.030,0.090) tip=(0.010,-0.030,0.060) mirror color=1a1512
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.98 to=1.10 r=0.032 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(-0.030,-0.030,0.085) tip=(-0.010,-0.028,0.055) mirror color=1a1512

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — THE MAW IS THE FACE. All structure is PRIMS (no reference mesh, so
  # blob:face-bake cannot run; the gargoyle road). The face block below is
  # shrunk to a NUB so it emits nothing. Skull bone (0,1.506,0.500) ->
  # (0,1.647,0.765); `at=` is a fraction along it and `offset=` a world
  # displacement from that point.
  # Order matters: cranium and brow FIRST, then the jaw masses, then the dark
  # maw interior, then the teeth (so the teeth read as the nearest surface
  # inside the mouth), then the eyes last so the brow still shadows them.
  # ============================================================
  # Cranium: a small dome high and BACK. Deliberately not the fattest prim on
  # the head — the upper jaw is — because a maw-dominated skull means the
  # braincase is the minority mass. Semi (0.165, 0.158, 0.158), crown y 1.78.
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.150 wide=1.10 tall=1.05 deep=1.05 blend=0.006 offset=(0,0.030,-0.070)
  # Brow shelf: a wide flat ridge over the eyes, the heaviest brow in the cast.
  # Semi-height 0.032 makes it a SHELF, not a lump; it overhangs the eyes so
  # they sit in shadow.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 r=0.075 wide=1.55 tall=0.42 deep=0.75 blend=0.004 offset=(0,0.055,0.095)
  # Upper jaw: the dominant mass. Wide (0.209 half-width) and deep (0.194),
  # bottom at y 1.44 — the roof of the maw and the bed of the upper teeth.
  blob head on skull at=0.38 r=0.155 wide=1.35 tall=0.68 deep=1.25 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.015,0.130)
  # Lower jaw: DROPPED 0.28 m below the skull point and pushed forward, so the
  # gape between the jaws is ~0.10 m — the "huge gaping mouth" beat. Its top
  # (y 1.38) is the floor of the maw; its bottom (y 1.13) is the heavy
  # under-jaw that hangs in front of the chest.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 r=0.140 wide=1.25 tall=0.90 deep=1.20 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.280,0.180)
  # Jaw hinge: a mass at the back of the lower jaw, tying it to the skull so
  # the mandible does not read as a detached lump.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 r=0.085 wide=1.00 tall=1.20 deep=1.10 blend=0.005 offset=(0.130,-0.090,0.050) both
  # Maw interior: the dark cavity behind the teeth. Recessed (z 0.10 against
  # the jaw fronts' 0.83-0.93) so it reads as depth, not as a plug.
  blob head on skull at=0.35 r=0.130 wide=1.15 tall=0.85 deep=1.15 blend=0.006 offset=(0,-0.090,0.100) color=1a0808
  # Upper gum line: a thin dark bar along the upper jaw's lower edge. Painted
  # near-black so the tooth roots have something to sit in.
  bar head on skull from=0.38 to=0.38 r=0.022 wide=1.90 tall=0.35 deep=0.60 blend=0.003 offset=(0,-0.085,0.150) color=2a0d0d
  # Lower gum line.
  bar head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.022 wide=1.70 tall=0.35 deep=0.60 blend=0.003 offset=(0,-0.255,0.190) color=2a0d0d

  # UPPER TEETH: four pairs (offset.x mirrored by `both`), each a tapered cone
  # rooted inside the upper jaw (y 1.47) and reaching down to y ~1.37. They
  # interlock with the lower row, so the mouth reads as a trap rather than a
  # painted grin. Ivory, no glow.
  bar head on skull from=0.38 to=0.38 r=0.030 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.040,-0.090,0.170) tip=(0,-0.100,0.010) both color=e8ddc0
  bar head on skull from=0.38 to=0.38 r=0.034 r2=0.005 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.105,-0.090,0.165) tip=(0,-0.105,0.010) both color=e8ddc0
  bar head on skull from=0.38 to=0.38 r=0.032 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.160,-0.090,0.150) tip=(0,-0.095,0.005) both color=e8ddc0
  bar head on skull from=0.38 to=0.38 r=0.026 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.205,-0.090,0.120) tip=(0,-0.080,0.000) both color=e8ddc0
  # LOWER TEETH: three pairs pointing UP from the lower jaw (y 1.35 -> 1.44),
  # plus two heavy canines at the corners of the maw.
  bar head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.030 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.040,-0.250,0.215) tip=(0,0.095,-0.005) both color=e8ddc0
  bar head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.032 r2=0.005 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.105,-0.250,0.210) tip=(0,0.100,-0.005) both color=e8ddc0
  bar head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.028 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.165,-0.250,0.185) tip=(0,0.090,-0.010) both color=e8ddc0
  # Canines: the heavy pair that make the maw read as a predator's, longer and
  # set at the corners where the jaw hinge is.
  bar head on skull from=0.22 to=0.22 r=0.040 r2=0.005 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.205,-0.245,0.155) tip=(0,0.135,-0.015) both color=e8ddc0

  # EYES — the lit pair, and the ONLY glow on this character (one authored
  # line, `both` doubles it; the pack allowlist pins the count at two). r 0.026
  # is small on purpose: against a 0.40 m maw the ratio IS the animal read.
  # Amber, deliberately not the gargoyle's ember orange, the cyberdemon's cyan
  # or the minotaur's red.
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.026 r2=0.012 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.085,0.030,0.085) tip=(0.006,-0.008,0.022) both color=ffcc22 glow=0.9

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB. headRadius 0.001 kills the emitted skull
# ellipsoid pair; browHeavy/noseLength 0 gate the emitted brow and nose off
# (facePrims emits only while those are > 0.0005). The head is authored prims
# above; this keeps the block present (and the lab's face panel live) without
# imposing the house oval. Same trick as gargoyle.blob.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# Raw-meat brute hide: dark red-brown linear base (the shader sRGB-encodes and
# lifts the low channels hard, so the numbers read darker than they render).
# Deliberately NOT the zombie's pink and NOT the minotaur's bright wet pink —
# this animal is grimy and matte. mottleColor is OLIVE (hue-shifted, not just
# darker) so the variation reads as dirt ON the hide rather than as meat IN it;
# mottleScale 2.6 puts the patches a hand-span across. Wound interior red.
palette
  baseColor     0.300 0.150 0.120
  deepColor     0.520 0.070 0.070
  charColor     0.080 0.050 0.040
  specIntensity 0.55
  specRoughness 0.46
  fresnelBoost  0.30
  translucency  0.10
  wetness       0.30
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.07
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.55
  mottleScale   2.6
  mottleColor   0.100 0.110 0.055
